---

Everything in this repository is synthesised from code: there are no
recorded samples. Rendered audio produced by the kit is a build product of
the recipes and code that made it.

---

Third-party code

The DX7 modes (addons/audio_kit/synth/synth_core.gd: classes _Dx7, _Dx7P,
_Dx7Lfo and the dx7_* functions; native/src/synth.cpp: Dx7Env, Dx7PEnv,
Dx7Lfo and the dx7_* functions; the algorithm table in
addons/audio_kit/synth/patch_lib.gd) are ports of parts of msfa, the synth
engine in Dexed (https://github.com/asb2m10/dexed, commit fea2f0f):
msfa/env.cc, pitchenv.cc, lfo.cc, freqlut.cc, sin.cc, fm_core.cc and
dx7note.cc, Copyright 2012 Google Inc. and Copyright 2017 Pascal Gauthier,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. tools/dx7_env_ref builds
msfa's own sources (not included here) to produce the reference values in
tests/data/dx7_env_ref.json and tests/data/dx7_ref.json. Dexed's "Mark I"
engine (GPL-3) is not used.

The granular effect (native/src/fx.h: the GR_* constants, gr_window,
setup_g, recoef_g, gr_start, tick_granular, gr_hermite, gr_reverb;
addons/audio_kit/dsp/stream_fx.gd: their GDScript twins) is a port of
the granular mode of Mutable Instruments Clouds
(https://github.com/pichenettes/eurorack, commit f4cfa76, clouds/dsp:
granular_processor.cc,
granular_sample_player.h, grain.h, audio_buffer.h, fx/diffuser.h,
fx/reverb.h, fx/fx_engine.h, resources/lookup_tables.py), used under
