Third-party data

addons/audio_kit/speech/data/en_stress.txt and en_stress.res (the
pseudo-speech stress dictionary), and docs/stress/held_out.txt, are built
by tools/build_stress_dict.py from these sources:

- Word frequencies from the Leipzig Corpora Collection (eng_news_2023_1M,
  https://wortschatz.uni-leipzig.de/en/download/English), licensed under
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
  D. Goldhahn, T. Eckart and U. Quasthoff, "Building Large Monolingual
  Dictionaries at the Leipzig Corpora Collection: From 100 to 200
  Languages", LREC 2012. Used at build time only, to choose which words
  ship; no frequency data is redistributed.
- Moby Pronunciator II and Moby Hyphenator II by Grady Ward (Project
  Gutenberg ebooks #3205 and #3204), in the public domain: stress for words
  CMU lacks and a cross-check against CMU (the Hyphenator's spelling splits
  are supported by the build script but not used in the shipped build).
- The CMU Pronouncing Dictionary (https://github.com/cmusphinx/cmudict),
  the stress for most words, used under this licence:

